# Story: someone who needs a terminal for ten seconds, many times a day, binds a key to `summon Terminal`.
# It comes over whatever is in view with the keyboard in it, goes when they turn away, remembers its place, and
# never moves the view. A note-taking app that is not even running is opened and summoned.
# Reference: F53 (A53 in collab/parity.json). Window ids start at 101.
open Editor
open Browser
open Terminal 400x300
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
focus 101
zoom
expect fills 101
expect hidden 103
# The key, pressed: Terminal is over the editor. Nothing else moved.
summon Terminal
expect ok
expect summoned 103
expect visible 103
expect in-front 103
expect fills 101
expect camera 101
# Pressed again: gone.
summon Terminal
expect ok
expect hidden 103
expect fills 101
# It is put where it is wanted, once.
summon terminal
move 103 40 560 1360 300
# A click on the editor sends it away.
focus 101
expect hidden 103
# In another view it comes to the same place.
neighbor right
neighbor right
expect fills 102
summon com.example.terminal
expect visible 103
expect fills 102
summon Terminal
# Sent away it is out of view everywhere, also where the Desktop shows: or the key would do nothing there.
show-all
expect hidden 103
desktop
expect hidden 103
summon Terminal
expect visible 103
summon Terminal
expect hidden 103
# ⌃⌥0 is the way back for a window that cannot be found, without exception: it is on the Desktop again.
home
expect visible 103
expect floating 103
summon Terminal
summon Terminal
expect hidden 103
# Switching to it some other way (⌘Tab, the Dock) summons it, and the view stays.
show-all
focus 103
expect summoned 103
expect camera root
focus 102
expect hidden 103
# An app that is not running is opened, and its window summoned when it appears.
zoom 101
summon Notes
expect ok
open Notes 300x400
expect summoned 104
expect fills 101
# One at a time: Terminal replaces Notes.
summon Terminal
expect summoned 103
expect hidden 104
# A docked window has a place, and the place wins.
summon Browser
expect ok
expect visible 102
expect docked 102
expect hidden 103
expect focused 102
# Again, and it is back where you were.
summon Browser
expect ok
expect focused 101
expect hidden 102
# Arranging leaves them out. Floating everything is a normal Mac again.
arrange
expect count docked 2
float-all
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
expect floating 103
